course: dictionary
lesson: 4623
title: Words from long ago
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a certain time. You can find out when a story happens by the words the writer uses. «Highwaymen shouted «Stand and deliver!» and robbed coaches.» Coaches and shouted orders on the road tell you this is an old story, long before cars.
explain: A highwayman was a robber on horseback who stopped travellers on the road and took their money. Look at the word itself: highway is a road, and a highwayman worked on the road. Use the clues around the word, such as horses and coaches, to check you have the right idea.
explain: Ask yourself: would people say this today? Highwayman is a story word. It is not used for a modern robber, so if you read about one in a news report, something odd is going on. Good readers notice when a word does not fit its time.
fact: A highwayman was a robber on horseback who stopped travellers on the road and took their money.
fact: Highwaymen lived in the old days, and you will meet them in history lessons, old stories, poems and plays.
fact: «Stand and deliver!» is what highwaymen shouted when they stopped a coach.
fact: The plural of highwayman is highwaymen.
fact: Highwayman is a story word, not used for modern robbers.
exercise: What is a highwayman? | *A robber on horseback who stopped travellers on the road and took their money | A shopkeeper who sold bread at the market | A knight who guarded the castle gate | A driver who goes too fast on the motorway
exercise: «Stand and deliver!» is what a highwayman shouted. What does this tell the reader? | The story is about a football match | The story is set in a modern city bank | *The story is set long ago, with horses and coaches | The story is set at a busy motorway service station
exercise: A news report says a highwayman robbed a bank in town today. Why does this seem odd? | Newspapers never use long words | Highwaymen only robbed shops, never banks | Banks are always closed on Tuesdays | *Highwayman is a story word for old-time road robbers, not modern ones
test: What is the plural of highwayman? | highwayers | highwaymanns | *highwaymen | highwaymans
test: What did highwaymen do to coaches? | Parked them in garages | Built them in factories | *Robbed them | Painted them bright red
exam: What does the word highwayman tell the reader about a story? | It is set in a school playground | *It is set in the old days, with horses and coaches | It is set on a modern motorway with lorries | It is set in a space station
